"""A vowel-to-vowel join between adjacent word fragments.

The main signal is a Latin or Cyrillic vowel ending one token and a vowel
starting the next, without a space. Short fragments and particular vowel
pairs are stronger; camel-case joins and qu endings are weaker. A separate
rule covers Arabic fathatan immediately after alif. This approximates the
positive signal, not the component's smaller, token-specific fluctuations.
